Local patches (some commits include related package changes):
- 2026-10-03 backdropShrinkRim: LiquidGlassSettings.backdropShrinkRim
  (0 to 1, default 0 = the upstream behaviour, bit for bit: the shader
  branch is skipped). The backdrop shrinks about the nearest point of a
  line through the material center along the longer side of the layer's
  glass bounds, rim x (long side - short side) long, instead of about
  the center: at 1 a capsule minifies by depth below its rim, as UIKit's
  lifted lens does. New uniform uBackdropShrinkAxis (vec2, float indices
  63-64, written with the common uniforms and on geometry bind);
  liquid_glass_settings.dart, rendering/liquid_glass_layer.dart,
  shaders/liquid_glass_final_render_core.glsl.
  backdropSamplingReach still assumes the center (an over-estimate).
- 2026-10-03 moved into the package: imports rewritten to
  package:morph/src/glass/renderer/, flutter/material swapped for
  flutter/widgets (GlassGlow's default glow is Color(0x3DFFFFFF), the
  value of Colors.white24), a catch clause given its `on Object`, asset
  keys under packages/morph/, the bundle renamed morph_glass.shaderbundle,
  dart format.
- 2026-10-03 web stubs: the three final-render .frag files compile to an
  empty shader under SKIA_GRAPHICS_BACKEND (the web's SkSL compiler
  rejects the core's texture sampling: "Only simple shader sampling is
  supported"); the web never draws liquid glass.
- 2026-10-03 field geometry: LiquidGlassLayer.field (GlassField,
  glass_field.dart) - a sampled signed distance field of one body its
  owner fused already; the geometry pass then runs
  shaders/gpu/geometry_field_fragment.glsl (new bundle entry
  GeometryFieldFragment) instead of the shape pass: the same matte
  encoding, distance / normal / half thickness interpolated bilinearly
  from an RGBA32F texture of the field's nodes (sampled nearest, so no
  float filtering is needed), uploaded through a small ring of
  host-visible textures written again only three frames after their
  last use. The material pass still reads the shapes.
- 2026-10-03 fake glass draws the fused outline: GlassField.outline (the
  traced zero contour, layer coordinates) is handed by LiquidGlassLayer to
  ConsolidatedFakeGlassLayer (`outline`), which then clips its backdrop
  and surfaces to it and tints the part no shape covers (the neck) like
  the first shape; without an outline it is upstream's per-shape union.

- 2026-10-04 WP-I runtime capability: the GPU context, shader bundle and
  final programs resolve once before morph reports liquid availability.
  Precaching before runApp does not await an application frame.
  Failed geometry bundle futures remain cached. Unavailable runtimes draw
  the frosted tier; the adaptive host follows readiness. Initialization
  failures report once through FlutterError.reportError in every build mode
  (library morph glass), with the cached reason exposed by
  MorphGlassRenderer.liquidUnavailableReason.
- 2026-10-04 WP-I packaging: the build hook creates build/shaderbundles/
  under the package root on every run (the pubspec asset entry always
  resolves) and, for native targets only, compiles
  morph_glass.shaderbundle into it (flutter_gpu_shaders, legacy mode);
  web targets skip compilation and compiler failures are logged, both
  leaving liquid unavailable. The runtime key is
  packages/morph/build/shaderbundles/morph_glass.shaderbundle. (A
  data-asset-only variant shipped no bundle on iOS/macOS: Flutter 3.47.2
  stable does not request data assets from hooks, so the device fell
  back to frosted - reverted the same day after the device audit.)
- Dependencies imported with the original package move: equatable,
  flutter_shaders, logging, flutter_gpu_shaders and hooks, plus Flutter GPU
  from the Flutter SDK. The unused logging dependency is now removed.
- 2026-10-04 WP-I removals: liquid_glass_blend_group.dart (including
  GlassGroupLink), liquid_glass_capture.dart, internal/capture_pass.dart,
  stretch.dart, internal/glass_drag_builder.dart, upstream glass_glow.dart
  (including three controllers per surface), logging.dart, precache.dart
  (replaced by the capability probe) and the geometry
  debug painter. LiquidGlass retains only the constructor morph uses;
  grouped/auto/own-layer constructors and their group/capture wiring are
  removed. renderer.dart exports only the retained shading API.
  LICENSE, NOTICE and third_party notices remain.
- 2026-10-04 WP-I content copies: one mounted consumer subtree records a
  vector picture for plain/offset-layer content. Other composited content
  uses one current-frame image, at the view's pixel ratio. Slot clips and
  the three rim-compensation transforms replay that source before lens
  glass. Copies have no hit testing or semantics. Resting content has no
  capture; no per-slot Path.combine remains.
- 2026-10-04 WP-I field uploads: an exact-sized, bounded four-texture ring
  replaces capacity uploads and staging copies; disposal releases host
  references. Flutter GPU requires full-mip overwrite, so each upload is
  exactly the active field. No field samples or shader optics changed.
- 2026-10-04 WP-I hygiene: local cascades become statements, source text is
  ASCII, outline clipping is shared, uniform circular distance-field
  corners are asserted, and renderer approximations are named engineering
  defaults. The sampled-field B-spline tracer remains separate from the
  engine's analytic-field tracer; its scratch buffers retain their high
  water mark, while the outline memo retains only four entries.
- 2026-10-04 WP-I diagnostics: backdrop-capture counts are opt-in, with a
  morph-prefixed message. Intentional independent lens and chrome passes
  do not produce automatic warnings.
- 2026-10-05 glass shadow clip: a GlassShadow with an offset shadow clips
  its shadows to outside the shape (an even-odd path of the shadow bounds
  and the shape deflated by half a pixel) instead of drawing them into a
  saveLayer and cutting the shape out with dstOut: no offscreen pass per
  shadowed surface, no shadow under the glass; only the antialiasing at
  the cut differs (flutter_test: <= 1 channel off the edge,
  test/glass_body_shadow_test.dart).
- 2026-10-05 live shapes and layers: LiquidGlass.live (a ValueListenable
  of LiquidGlassShapeFrame: shape, appearance, shadows) and
  LiquidGlassLayer.live (a Listenable with settingsOf / fieldOf) write each
  new frame straight into their render objects (RenderLiquidGlass, the
  glass shadow, the shape clip and visibility opacity, RenderFakeGlass,
  RenderLiquidGlassLayer, RenderConsolidatedFakeGlassLayer) through the
  GlassLiveBinding mixin (internal/glass_live.dart): the setters decide
  what changed, no widget rebuilds. The layer's scope carries the live
  settings (LiquidGlassRenderScope.settingsLive / currentSettings) for the
  shapes below it. A live shape rebuilds only when its kind of shape
  changes or its shadows appear or vanish; configurations no render
  object can follow (a standalone fake shape) rebuild per frame
  (GlassRebuildOn). GlassContentSource takes the same notifications to
  record its content again while a lens captures. The fixed constructors
  are unchanged and the same render objects are built either way, so the
  pixels are the same (test/glass_frames_test.dart).
- 2026-10-05 pipeline warm-up: internal/glass_warm_up.dart (new) draws
  every Flutter GPU pipeline of the geometry passes once (two 8 x 8
  renders through FlutterGpuGeometryRenderer.render) and rasterizes an
  offscreen layer scene with each final shader's backdrop filter (alone
  and composed over a mirror blur) and the frosted tier's blurs, clips,
  decorations and shadows, so the first glass frame creates no pipeline.
  Called from morphPrecacheLiquidGlass; failures are swallowed. No
  renderer source changed.
